course: dictionary
lesson: 1873
title: Working together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Collaboration is a noun. It means working together with others to make or do something. The verb is collaborate, to work together. The word has a lot of clues inside it, so look at the words around it to be sure which meaning is used.
explain: «Olympiads reward collaboration, not putting the other team down.» The clue is in the contrast: collaboration is set against putting the other team down. So collaboration must mean working together, helping each other, rather than beating others by being unkind.
explain: Other clues help too: group work, a project, a song sung by two people, or the phrase in collaboration with. A collaboration can also be a piece of work that people made together, like a joint painting or a shared report.
explain: In history, collaboration can have a very different and negative meaning: helping an enemy who has taken over your country. This is seen as wrong. If the story is about a war or an enemy army, read the clues carefully.
fact: Collaboration means working together with others to make or do something.
fact: «Collaboration» can also mean a piece of work made by people working together.
fact: In history, collaboration means helping an enemy who has taken over your country, and this is seen as wrong.
fact: Useful phrases: in collaboration with, close collaboration, a collaboration between.
fact: Teamwork is a close word for the first meaning, but collaboration is more formal and is often used in science, music and school projects.
exercise: «Olympiads reward collaboration, not putting the other team down.» What does collaboration mean here? | Beating others by being unkind | Running very fast alone | *Working together with others | Losing a game on purpose
exercise: The painting was a collaboration between Mia and Sam. What does collaboration mean here? | A picture of one person alone | *A piece of work made by people working together | A quarrel about who paints best | A paint shop
exercise: «The two scientists did their research in collaboration with a university.» Find and copy the one word that means working together. | *collaboration | university | research | scientists
test: In history, what does collaboration mean? | Playing a game with friends | *Helping an enemy who has taken over your country | Sharing your lunch with a classmate | Writing a story as a group
test: Mrs Green said, «The class worked in close collaboration with the library.» What does close collaboration mean? | Working alone in a quiet room | Being far away from the library | *Working together very closely | Arguing with the librarian
exam: Which of these is the best example of collaboration? | A teacher giving a test to one pupil | A child eating lunch alone at the back of the room | A dog barking at the postman | *Two scientists sharing their results to write one report together
